## Verification-only checks

- Verify `scripts/test-implement-anti-polling-rule.sh` still pins the live Step 5 breadcrumb in `skills/implement/SKILL.md`.
- If the breadcrumb changed, update the pinned literal.
- Update `docs/linting.md` only if the anti-polling harness text changes.
- Do not add new lint categories.

## Edge cases

- `skills/implement/SKILL.md` also matches the broad `skills/*/SKILL.md` rule.
- Direct-target dedup should keep target order stable.
- `design-step1d5.sh --mode collect` must reject zero paths.
- The new harness must not normalize zero paths into success.
- Dirty-tree sidecars may be absent.
- The clean checkpoint path should still write `RECOVERY_REQUIRED=false`.
- `LARCH_DYNAMIC_ARCHETYPES_MAX` may be set in `session-env.sh` and shell env.
- Preserve current precedence.
- `/bug` must be added in both bare and `larch:` strict-permission forms.
- OOS disposition checkpoint can fail after filing succeeds.
- Return non-zero and skip success markers so the Python path does not mark Step 9a.1 complete with unresolved disposition.
- The autofix ok path should write exactly one auto-fixed Warnings row.
- The autofix harness should assert the row in `execution-issues.md`.

## Failure modes

- A new Make target without shard wiring can fail harness shard coverage.
- A new harness without `python/checks.py` mapping can leave focused relevant checks incomplete.
- A README link to `docs/skills.md#bug` without a docs section creates a broken catalog link.
- Pairing `--stderr-sink` with canonical output files instead of failure logs can recreate the collect miss.
- A checkpoint call after `run-statistics.md` or manifest stamping can preserve false-complete state.
- A checkpoint call that reuses `finalize-state.sh` instead of the CLI can drift from the bash path.
- A broad upgrade cleanup glob can delete runtime files.
- A harness that expects the autofix ok-path Warnings row without wrapper emission will fail or pass vacuously.
- Keep cleanup patterns exact.

## Testing strategy

Run focused tests first:

- `make test-implement-structure`
- `make test-render-cost-line-callsites`
- `python3 -m pytest python/test_checks.py -q -k direct_targets`
- `make test-design-step-validator-autofix`
- `make test-design-step1d5`
- `make test-design-log-ship`
- `make test-review-and-fix-step5`
- `make test-implement-anti-polling-rule`
- `python3 -m pytest python/test_upgrade_larch.py -q`
- `python3 -m pytest python/test_oos_filer.py -q`
- `python3 -m pytest python/test_design_argv.py python/test_design_lifecycle.py python/test_design_log_publish_flow.py python/test_design_log_ship.py python/test_design_oos.py python/test_design_pause.py python/test_design_postplan.py python/test_design_publish.py python/test_design_step_log.py python/test_design_summary.py -q`
- Run the shard containing `test-design-step1d5`.
- Run the shard containing `test-design-log-ship`, for example `make test-harnesses-19` if that shard was used.
- `make test-harness-shards-coverage`

Then run required repo checks:

- `make lint`
- `make py-lint`
- `make py-test`

